  "executive_briefing": "Global tax and trade policy frameworks in late 2026 are undergoing critical structural transitions. The aggressive worldwide integration of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax is reshaping corporate tax strategies across more than 140 jurisdictions, with regions like ASEAN restructuring incentives to balance global compliance with local competitiveness. In corporate tax rates, major updates such as the U.S. One Big Beautiful Bill Act and regional adjustments in Europe highlight efforts to preserve revenue bases, alongside OECD data showing stable but complex tax regimes. In digital compliance, continuous transaction controls are maturing as Singapore enforces phased mandatory timelines for its Peppol-based InvoiceNow system. Meanwhile, unilateral trade policies face intense legal scrutiny, highlighted by the U.S. Court of International Trade declaring emergency-power tariffs unlawful while the global economy braced for potential 15-18% effective tariff averages.",
